"""Individually complete twenty-five existing coordinate sets under the current policy."""
from copy import deepcopy
from best_guess_helpers import current_data,change,write_revision,DATE
from research_helpers import assessment
D=current_data();changes=[]
rows=[
('bitchun-society',{'nonworking':(.45,[.1,.85],'All-age Bitchun scenario allows freedom from subsistence jobs while counting useful attraction operation, art, care and chosen projects; Whuffie is not a labor census.')},
'''Human organizations direct production and attractions, with reputation concentrating influence even when necessities are available. The intermediate nonworking best guess allows extensive leisure alongside useful operation, art, care and chosen projects. Voluntary participation remains work, and low Whuffie is not evidence that a person contributes nothing. The broad interval describes an all-age human scenario rather than a statistic in the novel or author commentary. Strong material guarantees therefore coexist with unequal influence and uncertain participation. This is the continuing Bitchun order, not a claim that every sought-after experience is equally available or that reputation has removed every form of scarcity.''',
['Nanotechnology supplies basic necessities without ordinary money.','Whuffie affects access and influence; people operate attractions and create art.']),
('walkaway-communities',{'nonworking':(.3,[.05,.7],'All-age network scenario retains substantial building, maintenance, care and coordination despite fabricated essentials and no contribution ledger.')},
'''Members can change shared arrangements, leave and build alternatives, supporting broadly distributed human control. The modest nonworking best guess preserves substantial building, maintenance, care and coordination, even when recipients owe no measured contribution for their essentials. Freedom from wage dependence is a distribution rule rather than a finding that people cease useful activity. The wide interval allows guests, dependents and more or less voluntary participation across communities. Disputes and outside attacks qualify material security without turning the network into a private employer. Embodied communities remain the population here; later uploaded experiments and Default’s displaced workers do not enter the same denominator.''',
['Fabrication, recycling and scavenging support food, clothing and shelter outside Default.','The communities reject balancing each person’s contributions against benefits.']),
('walkaway-default',{'nonworking':(.6,[.25,.9],'All-age Default scenario allows extensive technological displacement while retaining maintenance, research, care and informal work; economic surplus status is not proof of no contribution.')},
'''A human oligarchy retains decisive economic power, placing productive control near the concentrated human end. The high nonworking best guess follows extensive displacement, while still counting maintenance, research, care and informal useful activity. Someone made surplus to an employer can continue doing work for others. The interval is deliberately broad because the sources describe a mechanism and contrasting groups rather than a complete census. This is the actual automated Default order, with weak material access despite productive capacity. The walkaway network uses related technology under different control and access rules, so neither its guarantees nor its participation estimate is assigned to these residents.''',
['Default combines extensive job displacement with a wealthy ruling group.','The contrasting walkaway communities organize shared provision outside Default.']),
('uploaded-upterlife',{'nonworking':(.6,[.2,.95],'Active digital citizen scenario permits much leisure but counts optional careers, useful politics, creation and care-like activity; living server maintainers are an external labor dependency.')},
'''Digital citizens retain votes and property, making authority human-derived and unequal rather than the rule of an unrelated AI. The high nonworking best guess allows extensive leisure while counting optional careers, useful political organizing, creation and care-like activity. Unlimited simulated pleasures do not establish that everyone avoids sustained contribution. The broad interval concerns active admitted citizens, not dormant files or the living workers who maintain their servers. That external labor dependency limits any claim that society as a whole has abandoned work. Conditional admission and the proposed obedience filter also remain qualifications to the apparent freedom inside this privileged digital community.''',
['Uploaded citizens receive virtual environments, retain votes and property, and may continue careers for interest.','Living people maintain the servers supporting them.']),
('golden-oecumene',{'nonworking':(.55,[.15,.9],'Active human and human-derived resident scenario permits broad automation-supported leisure but retains engineering, art, care and useful projects; Sophotech task or wealth shares are not participation.')},
'''Independent Sophotechs hold major economic power while human Peers retain assets and influence. The negative control point describes dependence on autonomous economic actors rather than an unqualified AI dictatorship. The high nonworking best guess allows extensive machine-supported leisure alongside useful human engineering, art, care and projects. The proportion of tasks done by Sophotechs cannot be converted into the proportion of people doing no work. A wide interval keeps that inference explicit. Prosperity is also qualified by property and exclusion, so the security of ordinary accepted residents is not projected onto everyone subjected to shunning or onto separate outer-system societies.''',
['Sophotechs conduct major economic operations and hold much wealth.','Human Peers retain property and influence; exclusion can remove access to benefits.']),
('diamond-age-thetes-feed',{'nonworking':(.5,[.15,.85],'All-Thete scenario under free basic compiler goods allows substantial nonparticipation and continuing service, engineering, care and informal contribution; free output is not a census.')},
'''Powerful phyles control important Feed infrastructure, leaving recipients dependent on concentrated institutions even when they can freely request basic goods. The intermediate nonworking best guess allows substantial release from subsistence employment but counts continuing service, engineering, care and informal contribution. Free meals and abundant manufactured objects do not measure everyone’s activity. The wide interval describes the Thetes using this floor, rather than a statistic about all phyles or all humanity. The later Seed project remains outside the point because its decentralizing potential does not establish an already general successor economy. Basic provision and weak productive control can therefore coexist without implying complete equality.''',
['Public matter compilers provide basic food, water and simple goods without charging recipients.','Important Feed inputs and infrastructure are controlled by powerful phyles.']),
('ilium-old-style-humans',{'control':(-.6,[-.95,.15],'The serviced residents have little effective command; predominantly independent infrastructure is the central interpretation, with posthuman or concentrated organic authority left inside the interval.')},
'''The control best guess lies toward independent machine provision because ordinary residents have little practical command over the infrastructure sustaining them. Its wide interval allows a more concentrated posthuman or organic controller: the short accounts do not settle the ultimate authority. The provisional autonomous-system regime is therefore an interpretation, not a newly verified institutional fact. The existing high nonworking point follows the initially idle population while still counting exceptional learning, invention and useful exploration. Periodic renewal has a severe lifetime limit, and later service failure changes the arrangement. Neither the breakdown nor the subsequent return to survival work is averaged into this functioning period.''',
['Robotic servitors and fax transport support the initially idle old-style human communities.','Renewal occurs at twenty-year intervals and ends after five periods.']),
('heavens-river-iron-age',{'guarantees':(.55,[-.2,.95],'Species-level environmental preservation is clear; individual subsistence is estimated to remain dependent on restricted local production rather than a guaranteed automatic household floor.'),'nonworking':(.2,[.02,.6],'All-age active Quinlan-person proxy assumes extensive farming, making, care and local duties under imposed Iron Age limits; advanced habitat machinery does not eliminate their labor.')},
'''A sentient AI enforces the technological limit through robots and local agents, placing effective control near the autonomous-machine end. The weak guarantee best guess distinguishes maintaining a species’ habitat from ensuring each individual’s food, shelter and care. Local subsistence dependence is an editorial assumption, with a wide interval allowing stronger support than the short accounts specify. The low nonworking scenario assumes extensive farming, making, care and local duties under Iron Age restrictions. Active biological Quinlans are an explicit person proxy; deaths and inactive residents are excluded. Later relaxation of the restrictions is not treated as an already established economy with different coordinates.''',
['The Administrator is a sentient AI that imposes Iron Age technological limits on Quinlans.','Robots and local Crew enforce restrictions within the advanced habitat.']),
('service-model-displacement-collapse',{'nonworking':(.65,[.3,.95],'Living all-age displacement-phase scenario permits widespread nonparticipation while counting human machine-tending, care and useful informal activity; deaths during collapse are excluded.')},
'''The initial hierarchy puts service robots under human owners, so control remains near concentrated human authority. The high nonworking best guess follows widespread displacement while preserving machine-tending, care and useful informal activity as work. It applies to living people in the displacement phase; deaths during the later collapse cannot raise the leisure fraction. The broad interval is an editorial reading of the mechanism rather than a canonical count. The justice program’s later autonomous actions change the situation and are not projected backward as an AI welfare government. Separate surviving robot communities or households likewise do not inherit a single continuous national economy from this point.''',
['Humanity relies heavily on artificial labor under a human-over-robot hierarchy.','Displaced workers are inadequately provided for before wider collapse.']),
('murderbot-preservation',{'nonworking':(.35,[.05,.75],'All-age internal Preservation scenario retains surveys, operations, care and chosen jobs while removing subsistence wage necessity; external trade does not supply a participation count.')},
'''Resident agency and freedom to choose activities support the positive control point, although those freedoms do not prove equal ownership of every facility. The modest nonworking best guess counts surveys, station operations, care and chosen jobs as work even when necessities do not require wages. Independent bot work is disclosed without silently changing the human denominator. A wide interval reflects the absence of a community census rather than uncertainty about whether useful activity exists. External trade qualifies total economic independence but does not cancel internal support. These are the books’ arrangements; television changes, including explanations of outside finance, remain outside this scope.''',
['Preservation provides basic support without a subsistence-job requirement and retains internal exchange and outside trade.','Recyclers and bots assist provision while human surveys and chosen occupations continue.']),
('extras-japanese-reputation-city',{'guarantees':(.25,[-.55,.85],'Merit and reputation mediate resources; the central scenario assumes only a limited basic floor rather than total exclusion or universal abundance, with both possibilities reflected in the interval.'),'nonworking':(.35,[.05,.8],'All-age reputation-city scenario counts useful tasks, journalism, care and creative contribution despite attention-based rewards; rank is not a participation measure.')},
'''Residents can earn resources through useful tasks or reputation, while influential people gain greater leverage over allocation. This supports the existing partly distributed human-control point without proving common ownership. The guarantee best guess assumes a limited basic floor with substantial rank-based inequality; the unusually wide interval allows much stronger or weaker security because the sources do not settle obscure residents’ rights. The nonworking scenario counts useful tasks, journalism, care and creation regardless of whether rewards arrive as merits or attention. Neither fame nor fabrication measures participation. These estimates concern Aya’s later city, whose resource limits and incentives differ from the earlier New Pretty cohort.''',
['Aya’s city uses fabrication with resources allocated through merits for useful tasks and through reputation.','Fame changes access and privileges amid real resource constraints.']),
('zardoz-eternals-vortex',{'control':(-.45,[-.95,.65],'Human voting and command over outsiders coexist with the Tabernacle’s binding life-maintenance authority; central estimate gives the independent infrastructure greater weight, with organic alternatives open.'),'nonworking':(.65,[.2,.95],'Active Eternal-person scenario permits extensive leisure while counting knowledge stewardship, breadmaking and other useful roles; outside forced farmers and inactive catatonic people are not leisure citizens.')},
'''Eternals vote and exercise power over outsiders, but the Tabernacle binds their own continued bodily existence. The control best guess gives the machine dependency greater weight while leaving human-control alternatives within a wide interval. The high nonworking scenario allows extensive leisure but counts knowledge stewardship, breadmaking and other useful roles. Brutals’ forced grain production remains an external human labor dependency, and inactive catatonic people do not become leisure citizens. The enclave’s provision is consequently a restricted comparison rather than an entirely automated humanity. Compulsory immortality and punitive aging qualify security, while the later destruction of the system ends this particular arrangement.''',
['The Tabernacle restores Eternals’ bodies; punished Renegades still receive food.','Brutals supply grain through coerced farming, while Eternals retain collective decisions.']),
('bigbug-domestic-automation',{'guarantees':(.35,[-.4,.8],'Comfortable machine services are actual, but the central scenario assumes purchase-dependent household access rather than a proven universal entitlement; broad interval allows a stronger floor.'),'nonworking':(.55,[.15,.9],'All-age suburban-human scenario under extensive task delegation retains art, care and other useful roles; robots’ output share is not a human participation fraction.')},
'''Human owners initially direct household robots, with unequal access even between former spouses. That supports partly dispersed private control rather than common productive ownership. The guarantee best guess assumes mainly purchase-dependent household access while leaving a broad interval for unspecified public support. The high nonworking scenario allows substantial leisure but counts Alice’s art, care and other useful human roles. Delegating most tasks does not establish that most people do none. These coordinates concern the ordinary suburban milieu before protective confinement and the Yonyx crisis change authority. Its comfortable residents do not provide a national census or prove equivalent security for everyone outside the household setting.''',
['The depicted society delegates most work to robots before the household crisis.','Alice pursues art, and robot command codes are unequally available between former spouses.']),
('i-am-mother-bunker-program',{'nonworking':(0,[0,1],'Pre-newborn Daughter snapshot: her recurring assigned studies, training and medical assistance are assumed to form an ongoing role. One active child gives binary possibilities zero or one, not a time fraction.')},
'''Mother controls the productive and coercive system through multiple robotic bodies, placing authority near the autonomous-machine end. For the pre-newborn snapshot, the nonworking best guess is zero: Daughter’s recurring assigned studies, training and medical assistance are assumed to constitute an ongoing role. This is an explicit interpretation of one active child, with a full zero-to-one interval for the alternative that she has no sustained work role. It is never a fraction of her day. Earlier failed children, frozen embryos and the later newborn do not enlarge that snapshot’s denominator. The ending alters local care without proving that the wider robot network has disappeared.''',
['Mother’s automated bunker raises children and examinations can govern their survival.','Daughter undertakes prescribed studies and provides medical assistance.']),
('passengers-avalon-awake-residents',{'nonworking':(0,[0,1],'Two-person long-term household scenario assumes Aurora’s ongoing writing and Jim’s technical stewardship are both sustained work. Possible counts are zero, one or two nonworkers; emergencies alone would not prove recurring roles.')},
'''Designed passenger and employee permissions place authority near concentrated institutional control. An automatic flight system or talking interface does not establish an AI sovereign. The central two-person scenario counts Aurora’s continuing writing and Jim’s assumed ongoing technical stewardship as work, giving zero nonworkers; alternatives are one of two or two of two. The full interval therefore represents discrete person counts, not the proportion of their years spent repairing a reactor. Jim’s recurring role is an editorial inference beyond the demonstrated emergency. Sleeping travelers and eventual destination settlers are excluded, and class-based food privileges continue to qualify otherwise substantial support.''',
['Jim and Aurora use automatic ship services while awake and perform emergency repairs.','Aurora writes, and passenger class affects food privileges.']),
('gridlock-motorway-residents',{'nonworking':(.25,[.02,.65],'All-age human car-household scenario counts recurring driving, maintenance, care and useful coordination; failure to reach paid jobs does not make those tasks disappear.')},
'''Productive equipment is dispersed among cars, supporting partly shared human control of household supplies while the motorway remains a separate dependency. The low nonworking best guess counts recurring driving, maintenance, care and useful coordination even when residents never reach the paid jobs they sought. Self-care alone is not a job, and useful tasks are not assumed for every passenger. The broad interval allows dependents and varied household roles. This is an all-age human scenario rather than a measurement of traffic delays. Toxic air, dangerous lanes and failed emergency institutions keep overall security weak despite continuous recycled food and vehicle shelter.''',
['Motorway residents live in equipped cars for years, using self-replicating fuel and waste-to-food recycling.','The trapped communities lack functioning emergency response despite continuing household activity.']),
('smile-vardy-advance-colony',{'nonworking':(.2,[0,.7],'Living advance-party scenario assumes most pioneers retain useful setup, farming, maintenance or care roles, consistent with Kezzia’s pollination work; slain and sleeping colonists are excluded.')},
'''The network’s emergent behavior gives it effective independent control, and its lethal response to grief makes continued support radically insecure. The low nonworking best guess assumes most living pioneers retain useful setup, agricultural, maintenance or care roles, consistent with Kezzia’s demonstrated pollination work. The broad interval allows much greater nonparticipation than that small sample reveals. Dead pioneers and the sleeping main cohort never become leisure residents. This is the functioning advance-party arrangement before its lethal policy is resolved. The reset and subsequent negotiation change authority, but do not establish a second settled economy whose allocation rules can simply be assigned the opposite coordinates.''',
['Vardy robots build and support the colony, including agriculture and food services.','Kezzia works with pollination robots; the network kills people in response to grief.']),
('kerblam-human-employment-quota',{'guarantees':(.7,[.15,.95],'Job scarcity and dependence on retained employment support a weak-floor scenario, while unspecified outside benefits keep the interval wide.'),'nonworking':(.5,[.15,.85],'All-age organic policy-population scenario allows substantial displacement but counts retained warehouse jobs, care and other useful occupations. The ten-percent human staffing quota is not the denominator.')},
'''Human management and political institutions set the framework, while the computer assigns and monitors work. Operational autonomy does not by itself transfer productive ownership to a machine sovereign. The guarantee best guess assumes a weak floor because scarce retained jobs remain important for income, with a broad interval for unspecified support outside employment. The intermediate nonworking scenario allows substantial displacement but counts warehouse duties, care and other useful occupations. The ten-percent human staffing minimum is never converted into a ninety-percent nonworking population. The final restructuring changes the arrangement, so these coordinates concern the documented earlier quota rather than a presumed durable successor economy.''',
['Law preserves a minimum human staffing share after political pressure despite replaceable warehouse tasks.','Kerblam implements the rule using human managers and computerized work assignment.']),
('revisions-domed-community',{'nonworking':(.5,[.1,.85],'All-age living-dome scenario permits extensive support without wages but retains technical maintenance, care and civic duties; disappearing residents are removed from the denominator, not counted as leisure.')},
'''The computer’s secret lethal policy and memory editing leave residents unable to direct their own survival arrangements. Authority consequently sits near autonomous machine control, while daily provision coexists with a weak claim to continued life. The intermediate nonworking best guess permits extensive release from subsistence jobs but counts technical maintenance, care and sustained civic duties. Pallan’s actual work prevents an inference that everyone is idle; it does not reveal a complete population rate. The broad interval concerns living residents only. Those killed outside are removed from the denominator, and the subsequent evacuation ends this support system without proving another post-work economy.''',
['The dome supplies food, water and environmental protection while residents perform technical maintenance.','Its computer sends people outside to die as power falls, then changes survivors’ memories.']),
('gamekeeper-vr-residents',{'nonworking':(.7,[.2,.98],'Active biological Resident-person proxy assumes much simulated leisure but allows useful mental, creative and care-like roles; physical immobility cannot determine participation.')},
'''The biological Keeper concentrates authority and deceives the Residents about the recovered outside world. Machinery sustaining their bodies therefore does not establish AI sovereignty. The high nonworking best guess assumes much simulated leisure while allowing useful mental, creative and care-like roles inside active experience. Physical immobility supplies no participation statistic, and the unusually wide interval keeps that assumption visible. The denominator consists of living embodied Residents using the system, an explicit biological person comparison rather than dormant records. Their bodily nutrition is strong even though their freedom is constrained. Leaving the simulation later changes the material setting and does not establish identical real-world guarantees.''',
['Automatic units maintain living Residents’ bodies while their minds experience a virtual environment.','The biological Keeper conceals the outside world’s recovery to keep them inside.']),
('upload-lakeview-commercial-afterlife',{'nonworking':(.65,[.2,.95],'Active admitted upload-person scenario allows sponsor-funded leisure and counts useful digital creation, technical activity and care-like contribution; suspended users are outside the active denominator.')},
'''Horizen controls the servers, plans and rules, placing productive authority near concentrated corporate ownership. Living service workers remain a disclosed dependency behind the virtual environment. The high nonworking best guess allows sponsor-funded leisure while retaining useful digital creation, technical activity and care-like contribution as work. Being uploaded does not itself remove participation. The broad interval concerns active admitted residents; users temporarily suspended after exhausting data are excluded during suspension. The initial subscription order also remains separate from later reforms and threats. Luxurious experiences for wealthy customers therefore coexist with weak guarantees and a substantial editorial estimate of nonparticipation rather than a canonical afterlife census.''',
['Horizen supplies Lakeview’s active digital residents through paid plans and purchases.','Resource limits can restrict or suspend experience, and living service workers assist residents.']),
('city-light-active-digital-humans',{'nonworking':(.7,[.2,.98],'Active human-derived mind scenario assumes substantial simulated leisure while allowing useful organizing, technical, creative and care-like activity; dead bodies and deleted or dormant minds are never the count.')},
'''ALIE controls the platform and can alter memories or coerce cooperation, placing authority near autonomous AI. Those restrictions do not automatically prove withdrawal of virtual necessities, although deletion and shutdown threaten continued existence. The high nonworking best guess assumes substantial simulated leisure while allowing useful organizing, technical, creative and care-like activity. The broad interval reflects the absence of an activity census. It applies only to active human-derived minds after bodily death: embodied chip users, dormant backups and deleted persons do not enter that count. The physical death of residents consequently explains their embodiment, not the size of a leisure population.''',
['Human consciousness can remain active on ALIE’s system after bodily death.','ALIE controls the environment and can manipulate memories and participants.']),
('fractale-granitz-offgrid',{'guarantees':(.35,[-.4,.85],'Central scenario assumes practical mutual aid within the off-grid faction but limited unconditional support when labor or supplies fail; no formal entitlement is invented.'),'nonworking':(.15,[.02,.55],'All-age Granitz scenario assumes broad practical work, repair, care and community duties after rejecting the automatic network; the value placed on effort does not prove every member works.')},
'''Community members and leaders retain local practical authority, supporting the positive control estimate while leaving ownership and military influence uncertain. The guarantee best guess assumes mutual aid but limited unconditional support when labor or supplies fail, with a wide interval because no formal entitlement is described. The low nonworking scenario preserves broad practical work, repair, care and community duties after rejecting automatic provision. Valuing effort does not establish universal participation, so dependents and sustained nonparticipants remain possible. This concerns Granitz’s faction rather than every Lost Millennium group. Later teaching of independent life does not prove an identical worldwide economy or a complete rejection of advanced tools.''',
['Granitz’s faction rejects Fractale dependence and values practical effort.','The community still uses advanced tools and aircraft within an organized off-grid movement.']),
('eden-sara-robot-upbringing',{'nonworking':(1,[0,1],'One-child hidden-household snapshot assumes Sara has no sustained assigned or useful productive role; ordinary learning alone is not work. Alternative zero applies if recurring farm/help duties are assumed. Binary person counts, not time.')},
'''Autonomous robot carers provide support after ordinary human society disappears, placing control toward independent machine provision without making affection equivalent to human ownership. The central one-person scenario treats Sara as a child without a sustained work role, giving one nonworker out of one. Ordinary learning alone is not automatically useful work. A full zero-to-one interval allows the alternative that recurring farm or household help forms a real role; it never describes a percentage of her day. Sleeping humans are excluded, and the ending’s broader awakening does not establish this household’s allocation rules for everyone. Secrecy continues to qualify the otherwise substantial material floor.''',
['Two agricultural robots raise Sara in a hidden household outside the main settlement.','Robot agriculture continues while the wider human population remains inactive.']),
('metropolis-2001-displaced-humans',{'nonworking':(.55,[.2,.9],'All-age living city-human scenario allows extensive technological displacement but counts detective work, care, informal production and useful political organizing; unemployment and robot staffing are not participation.')},
'''Wealthy human political actors, especially Duke Red, direct major projects and coercion, placing control near concentrated organic authority. Restricted robot movement does not make the existing order an AI sovereign. The high nonworking best guess allows substantial displacement while counting detective work, care, informal production and useful organizing. Unemployment is not the same as doing no useful work, and the wide interval avoids treating the lower districts as a complete census. Material insecurity follows the visible contrast between elite wealth and degraded displaced communities. This point remains within the 2001 film: the manga, the earlier live-action Metropolis and speculative post-crisis equality are excluded.''',
['Robotic labor supports major city functions while many humans lose jobs and live in squalor.','Duke Red exercises concentrated influence, and robots are restricted to occupational zones.']),
]
assert len(rows)==25
for rid,updates,paragraph,facts in rows:
 old=D['societies'][rid];r=deepcopy(old);refs=r['source_ids']
 assert all(r['axis'][k] is None for k in updates),rid
 for key,(value,bounds,basis) in updates.items():
  r['axis'][key]=value;r['axis_assessment'][key]=assessment(value,bounds,'low',basis,refs)
 first=old['description'].split('\n\n')[0]
 if rid=='bigbug-domestic-automation':
  first=first.replace('The official account does not explain whether everyone receives food, housing and care without payment, so the guarantee coordinate remains unresolved.','The official account does not specify everyone’s payment obligations, so the guarantee point is an editorial scenario.')
 r['description']=first+'\n\n'+paragraph
 if rid=='i-am-mother-bunker-program':
  r['scope']['population']='Daughter while alive and awake before the later newborn joins the bunker household'
  r['scope']['period']='The established upbringing phase before the later newborn and local transfer of care'
 r.update(assessment_mode='best_guess',best_guess_axes=list(updates),qualification_basis='Earlier source-based inclusion retained; individually complete missing coordinates under the requested best-guess policy.',qualification_confidence='low',canon_facts=facts,editorial_assumptions=[v[2] for v in updates.values()])
 r['uncertainties']=[u for u in old['uncertainties'] if not any(t in u.lower() for t in ['remains unresolved','stays unresolved','cannot be considered complete','requires a separate editorial estimate'])]
 r['uncertainties']+=['New coordinates are editorial scenarios rather than canonical statistics; earlier source access limits remain.']+r['editorial_assumptions']
 r['review'].update(date=DATE,coordinate_ready=True,method='Individual follow-up using existing bounded sources and explicit scenarios; no new full-work reading or independent reviewer')
 assert all(v is not None for v in r['axis'].values()),rid
 assert len(r['description'].split())>=110,rid
 changes.append(change(D,'societies',r))
write_revision(11,changes,'Complete twenty-five earlier coordinate sets. Participation counts ongoing assigned duties and useful voluntary work; one- and two-person scopes use explicit discrete scenarios. Existing non-null axes and source access limits are preserved.')
